}}

==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Nezuko Kamado CC''' at level 10.

==Strategy/Usage==
Nezuko Kamado moves fast, attacks fast, and deals a lot of damage. However, she can [[Attacks Only|Only Attack]] [[:Category:Traitless Enemies|Traitless]], [[:Category:Alien Enemies|Alien]] and [[:Category:Zombie Enemies|Zombie]] enemies, which can make it difficult to use her to her maximum potential. She's not recommended for use in many mixed stages due to the presence of non-targets that outrange her.

In truth, her matchups against Traitless enemies are not very good; her bulk is too low to endure the wrath of an [[R.Ost]] or [[Rain D.]], she has no immunities to handle enemies like [[H. Nah]] or [[Mr. Mole]], and she pushes away tankier backliners such as [[Henry]] to a safer distance. She's best used against aggressive melee pushers like [[Dagshund]], [[Dober P.D]], as well as [[Kory]]. Put her in the ring with Aliens and she faces a similar problem, where most enemies that outrange her simply won't give her the time of day. Some Aliens in particular are especially unforgiving with their abilities, including [[:Category:Starred Alien Enemies|Starred Aliens]] with Warp and [[Barrier]]s. Nonetheless, she finds very decent use cases against the melees she does outrange in [[Nimoy Bore]], [[Elizabeth the LVIth]], [[General GreGory]], [[Mesocosmocyclone]], and others. This makes her somewhat decent for [[Into the Future]] and [[Cats of the Cosmos]].

Her best target by far are Zombies, whom she can effectively crowd-control and damage very reliably. She can prevent Zombies from burrowing either through sheer damage or the [[Knockback]] ability itself, and has [[Zombie Killer]] to finish them off then and there. Her range is just enough to outrange some of the most pesky Zombies like [[Zang Roo]] and [[Zir Zeal]], and better yet, she attacks fast enough to keep up with constant Zombie spam. She still finds immense trouble in dealing with enemies that outrange her even here (e.g. [[Lord Gravey]] and [[Cadaver Bear]]), but she fares far better than her other two targets.

Overall, Nezuko Kamado is a fairly middling unit despite her impressive offensive power, especially with [[Strengthen]]. She finds her best usage in niche situations with primarily heavy melee pressure.

